- What is `%cx` supposed to hold?
  Maybe `%cx` hold another thread turn (?).
- What is `.spin1` instructions about?
  It is the instructions to check whether another thread trying to access the
  critical section.
- What is `.spin2` instructions about?
  It is the instructions when another thread trying to enter critical section
  (after check on `.spin1`), and then we check if the `turn` value is the same
  as another thread's ID:
  - If it is the same, the current thread will not go into critical section and
    wait for the another thread to finish execute the critical section and
    release the lock.
  - If it is not the same, the current thread will go into critical section and
    the another thread will need to wait until the current thread finish execute
    the critical section and release the lock.

This peterson's algorithm works because of yield to the another thread
mechanism. If both threads trying to enter the critical section at the same
time, whichever thread yielded last will wait for another thread (?).

